happy Mother's Day when I was a kid  Mother's Day meant ridiculous crafts  poorly written cards that only a mother  could love and making an absolute mess  of the kitchen just trying to make mom  breakfast in bed some things never  change but what we are going to change  is that run-of-the-mill boxed crap  pancake breakfast in favor of some  protein packed versions so I pardoned up  with my friends at genuine health to  bring you protein pancakes three ways I  am so excited about this new line of  protein powder because unlike your  typical whey powder  it's made with grass-fed fermented dairy  protein and the fermentation helps you  absorb a better and digestive as well  in other words guys you get all the high  absorption benefits of a protein powder  like way but without the farty bloated  crappy Vitamix see mom I love you and I  love your guts  let's make pancakes first up my gluten  free strawberry cheesecake lemon  pancakes I add one and a quarter cups of  gluten-free oats to a food processor a  blender and pulse until they turn into a  powder then I mix together my powdered  oats a teaspoon of cinnamon one scoop of  vanilla genuine health fermented Greek  yogurt proteins plus powder vanilla  plain fat-free Greek yogurt skim milk  honey lemon zest an egg baking powder  and a pinch of salt I gently mix  ingredients together and allow the  batter to rest for about ten minutes  then I pour about a quarter cup of  batter into the pan and let it cook  now I'm a traditionalist so I'm all that  the round pancakes but if you want to go  crazy pants and bust out the molds and  little smiley face in there for Mom  hey go for it your pancakes your  prerogative so once you see the bubbles  form around the edges I just flip it and  continue to cook it until it's golden  brown on both sides  meanwhile in a food processor or blender  I puree the cream cheese yogurt lemon  zest and honey together and I set that  aside that is going to be our yummy  cheesecake filling I also cook down some  frozen strawberries with a little bit of  honey and water in a saucepot until it's  jammy and saucy then when it's time to  I dollop a few heaping spoonfuls of that  decadent cheesecake filling between my  pancakes and I just doused the whole  thing in this delicious strawberry sauce  next up is my black forest cake inspired  pancakes you start pretty much with the  same batter but - the lemon zest and I  add in a tablespoon of cocoa powder to  the mix I also do the sauce pretty much  with the same technique except where I  use dark cherries instead of the  strawberries and then I sweetened a  little bit of that Greek yogurt with a  touch of honey I layer them all together  and then I chop the whole thing off with  some decadent dark chocolate shavings  and finally my chocolate banana peanut  butter pancakes  these are heavenly so I start with the  same go-to protein pancake mix both out  the lemon zest and then I adding some  mini chocolate chips and some sliced  banana while they're cooking then for my  filling I whip together some Greek  yogurt with some natural peanut butter  and a touch of honey to sweeten and then  I topped the whole thing off with some  more sliced bananas some more chocolate  chips and some salted peanuts as well oh  yeah  it's a good one see the pancake  possibilities are endless so be sure to  leave me a comment below about what you  come up with for your mom and Mother's  Day well thanks so much for watching if  you like what you see of course be sure  to subscribe to my channel and like this  video share with your friends and your  mom and I'll see you next time on Abby's  kitchen
 

